script = ExtResource("1_f2ctb")
dialogue_id = "debate_royal_monument"
record_title = "Debate Speech: The Royal Monument"
text = "PAGE: historian(PORTAL_NETWORK), AUDIENCE
historian: I have recently heard of a curious monument on an otherwise ordinary shard.
historian: It is a metal statue of an ancient ruler, standing three stories tall.
historian: It makes me think of the labor and resources poured into such a project.
historian: It must have taken hundreds of people and enough metal to make ten thousand hammers.
historian: All to stoke one person's vanity.
historian: When we raise a person to a pedestal overlooking the entire world, their whims become the law of the land.
historian: When a leader governs millions, people become numbers in a ledger.
historian: They become resources to be allocated, and having a few hundred people forge a statue is hardly a significant expenditure.
historian: A society on that scale becomes a blind, hungry beast, uncaring of its own citizens.
historian: If we are led by one state, we will turn ourselves into fuel for another grand monument."
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://jtkfcsyiryo4"
